From: sgl-project/sglang PR #36743 (open upstream, branch
    jpezzulli/sglang:john/upstream-mamba-cow-load-order)
    "Order deferred mamba COW after an active HiCache layerwise load"
    Adapted to the qwen4-main-squashed fork tree (anchors verified against
    the sglang-official working tree on 2026-11-01).

Companion to 0012 (PR #36738). HiCache publishes restored radix slots while
their layerwise H->D transfer is still in flight; the deferred mamba COW in
_maybe_execute_deferred_mamba_cow_and_clear consumes a WHOLE slot, so it can
copy partial (not-yet-restored) mamba state. The per-layer counter only gates
the attention/linear layers, not the pre-forward COW. This adds the pool-side
wait-for-final-layer fence before the COW copy.

Hunks are upstream-identical (the fork's HybridReqToTokenPool lives in
memory_pool.py here, matching upstream paths; the model_runner COW block is
the fork's own but structurally identical).

